## §4. TESTING — Authoritative Suite, No Hiding Failures

- Authoritative command: `python -m pytest -q --color=no` (full suite per `pytest.ini` testpaths).
- FORBIDDEN: narrowing pytest scope to hide failures, running a subset while claiming full suite passes.
- All test markers MUST be registered in `pytest.ini`. New test files MUST use existing marker taxonomy.
- When tests disappear: check `pytest --collect-only -q` vs execution count. If counts differ, audit `conftest.py` `pytest_collection_modifyitems` hooks — they can silently deselect tests.
- Evidence MUST show "collected X / executed Y" counts. Any deselection must be explained.
- `pytest.ini` testpaths changes require same-commit update to `tests/unit_min_deps/test_testpaths_contract.py`.
- Phase completion requires: pytest exits 0, git status clean, evidence file committed.

